# Per-PR review-loop evidence: snapshots, the loop position, dispatch logs
# and exit files, under .agents/reviews/pr-<n>/.
#
# EPHEMERAL BY CONTRACT. A fresh container legitimately has none of it, and
# re-dispatching is the documented remedy rather than a workaround. What must
# survive a round is committed elsewhere: the adjudication record and its
# verdict in .agents/adjudications/, the budget receipt in .agents/receipts/,
# and the delivery line in .agents/deliveries.md.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The contract already said this directory was ignored,
# and it was not. plan-review.mjs writes an ignore file for the directories a
# PLAN loop creates; a CODE review loop never runs that script, so
# .agents/reviews/pr-<n>/ was covered by nothing and an ordinary `git add -A`
# staged a snapshot of the pull request body. (AI-Handbook #91 round 1.)
#
# WHY THERE ARE TWO COPIES. Git does not follow a symlinked .gitignore, so a
# pointer is impossible and a real file at each root is the only option. The
# handbook mirrors this one at .agents/reviews/.gitignore, and
# scripts/check-root-wiring.mjs compares the pattern lines so the duplication
# is enforced rather than merely intended. Edit THIS copy; the root follows.
*
!.gitignore
